  "summary": "The 62nd NHL Entry Draft was held June 28–29, 2024, at Sphere in Paradise, Nevada. Draft rights belonging to the deactivated Arizona Coyotes transferred to the Utah Hockey Club.\n\nThe San Jose Sharks won the first overall pick for the first time in franchise history and selected Macklin Celebrini. Chicago chose Artyom Levshunov second, and Anaheim selected Beckett Sennecke third. San Jose and Chicago won the two draft lotteries, but neither result changed the draft order—the first time that had happened since 2010.\n\nEligible players were generally born between January 1, 2004, and September 15, 2006, with additional eligibility for certain undrafted non-North American players and unsigned players from the 2022 draft. The article also details the round-by-round selections and numerous trades that changed which teams held picks, including trades involving first- and second-round selections.",
